  <section class="wrap fiche-body">
    <div>
      <p>Looking for a restaurant that accepts dogs in Port-Grimaud? Coco tested Le Grand Pin in person: dogs welcome on the terrace, right on the canals.</p>

      <h2>The vibe</h2>
      <p>In the heart of Port-Grimaud, almost with its feet in the water, Le Grand Pin serves traditional southern French cuisine on a covered terrace overlooking the port's canals — a pleasant spot to extend a stroll along the quays with your dog. The place mixes passing tourists with local regulars, a good sign of its consistency.</p>

      <h2>What to know before you go</h2>
      <p>Coco Explore ate here in person: very good food, a warm atmosphere, and two dogs settled at neighbouring terrace tables without any issue. According to an informal conversation on-site, dogs are welcome on the terrace, with no strict rule announced (size, muzzle) beyond ordinary common sense — it's best to simply mention it when you sit down. The restaurant takes no reservations (confirmed by the tourist office and by its own website, which also ticks "pets allowed" and terrace): you just show up, and if there's room, you eat.</p>
      <p>Worth checking before you go: opening days and dates. The tourist office (updated 11/09/2026) lists it open from 1 April to 30 September 2026, every day except Wednesday, 12pm to 2pm and 6.45pm to 9.15pm, marked "to be confirmed"; another tourist office listing mentions Saturday closed, and we had been told on site "until the end of October". The 2026 season is over: confirm 2027 dates on 04 94 54 89 72.</p>
      <div class="callout">Coco's tip: use the meal to extend your walk along the canals of Port-Grimaud, one of the few villages built around its own marina.</div>

      <h2>Frequently asked questions</h2>
      <h3>Are dogs allowed at Le Grand Pin?</h3>
      <p>Yes, on the terrace — seen in person by Coco Explore.</p>
      <h3>Do you need to book?</h3>
      <p>No, the restaurant takes no reservations (tourist office): first come, first served.</p>
      <h3>Is the restaurant open all year?</h3>
      <p>No, it is a seasonal restaurant (see the dates above); 2027 dates to be confirmed on 04 94 54 89 72.</p>

      <h2>Nearby</h2>
      <p>The medieval village of Grimaud and its dog-friendly restaurants (Le Café de France, La Baie des Voiles) are a few minutes away by car, up on the hillside.</p>
